1. Scope

This license applies to CWBridge material owned by its copyright holders,
including the application core, executable distributions, first-party launcher,
web interface, and protected project artifacts. CWBridge is proprietary software;
making interface source files publicly readable does not make it open source.

2. Permitted use

You may, without a license fee, install and use official CWBridge distributions
for personal or commercial purposes on devices you own or are authorized to use.
You may make copies reasonably required for that use and for backup. You may
read the publicly provided interface and launcher sources and modify them for
your own use. You may share complete, unchanged official distributions if this
license and all applicable copyright and third-party notices remain included.
These permissions do not grant trademark rights or any right to claim ownership.

3. Protection of the core

Except where mandatory applicable law permits it, or where a copyright holder
has given written authorization, you must not reverse engineer, decompile,
disassemble, decode, decrypt, or extract the core or protected project artifacts
to recover their implementation or source code. You must not circumvent their
technical protection for that purpose, publish recovered implementation material,
or distribute modified core binaries or works copying that protected implementation.
Redistribution of modified first-party source or modified distributions requires
the copyright holders' separate permission.

4. Mandatory legal rights

Nothing in this license excludes rights that applicable law makes non-waivable.
In particular, rights to make necessary backup copies, to observe, study or test
software during authorized use, to carry out legally permitted error correction,
and to perform qualifying decompilation for interoperability remain unaffected.
Where German law applies, this includes the relevant rights under sections 69d
and 69e UrhG and the limits on contractual restrictions in section 69g(2) UrhG.
This license does not prohibit independently developed software that does not
copy CWBridge's protected expression or otherwise infringe its rights.

5. Third-party components

Third-party components, fonts, icons, libraries and other material remain subject
to their own licenses. Their license terms and legally required notices take
